{
  "number": 528,
  "title": "Random Pick with Weight",
  "spec": "leetcode",
  "statement": "Write a class `Solution` that samples indices according to weights.\n\n- `new Solution(w)` receives `w`, an array of positive integers in which `w[i]` is the weight of index `i`.\n- `pickIndex()` returns one index from `0` to `w.length - 1`, chosen at random so that index `i` comes up with probability `w[i] / (w[0] + w[1] + ... + w[w.length - 1])`. Every call makes a new, independent choice.\n\nUse `Math.random()` for randomness; in this app it follows a fixed seed, so runs repeat exactly. Since many outputs are correct, an answer is accepted when the constructor gives `null`, every `pickIndex()` result is a valid index, and across the calls of a case each index is chosen about as often as its weight predicts (a generous statistical check).",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= w.length <= 10^4 (at most 2,000 here)",
    "1 <= w[i] <= 10^5",
    "pickIndex is called at most 10^4 times (at most 499 times per case here)"
  ],
  "signature": {
    "kind": "design",
    "name": "Solution",
    "constructor": "Solution(int[] w)",
    "methods": [
