  "notes": "## Intuition\n\nPicture the weights laid end to end on a number line: index 0 owns the first `w[0]` unit cells, index 1 the next `w[1]` cells, and so on, `total` cells in all. Choosing one cell uniformly at random lands in index `i`'s stretch with probability `w[i] / total`, which is exactly what is asked. The brute-force idea walks the stretches from the left until the cell is found, O(n) per pick. Storing the running sums (prefix sums) instead makes the stretch boundaries sorted, so binary search finds the owner in O(log n).\n\n## Approach\n\n1. In the constructor, add up the weights left to right and store each running sum in `prefix`; `total` is the last one.\n2. In `pickIndex()`, draw `target`, a whole number from `0` to `total - 1`.\n3. Index `i` owns the cells `prefix[i - 1] .. prefix[i] - 1`, so the answer is the first `i` with `prefix[i] > target`.\n4. Binary search for it with `left` and `right`: if `prefix[mid] > target` the answer is `mid` or earlier, otherwise it is after `mid`.\n5. Return `left` when the bounds meet.\n\n## Example 1, step by step\n\n`w = [1]`, so `prefix = [1]` and `total = 1`. Every `target` is `Math.floor(r * 1) = 0`; `left = right = 0`, the loop does not run, and `pickIndex()` returns `0`. For `w = [1, 3]` (Example 2), `prefix = [1, 4]`: `target = 0` gives index `0`, while `target` `1`, `2` or `3` gives index `1`, a 1 : 3 split.\n\n## Complexity\n\n- Time: O(n) for the constructor and O(log n) per `pickIndex()`.\n- Space: O(n) for `prefix`.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n- Search for `prefix[mid] > target`, not `>=`, when `target` starts at 0; otherwise every index steals one cell from the next.\n- Picking an index uniformly ignores the weights entirely.\n- Recomputing the sums in every `pickIndex()` call is O(n) per pick and too slow for many calls.\n\n## Variables\n\n| Name | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `prefix` | `prefix[i]` = `w[0] + ... + w[i]` |\n| `total` | sum of all weights |\n| `weight` | the weight being added in the constructor |\n| `target` | the random cell, from `0` to `total - 1` |\n| `left`, `right`, `mid` | binary search bounds over `prefix` |",
